qa/tts-audit-prod-gu-clips/

# Local secrets. Replit ignored these via a machine file that does not
# exist outside it, so the rule has to live in the repo. The glob is
# deliberately wide: .env.bak and .env.save slip past an explicit list, and a
# leaked key costs more than an ignored file nobody wanted ignored.
.env*
# Templates carry no secrets and must stay committed. Covers the root and
# artifacts/bolo-mobile/.env.production.example alike.
!.env*.example

# Signing and API private keys. The repo is PUBLIC, and every one of these is a
# credential that grants real access: a .p8 App Store Connect key can read and
# change the App Store listing, and a .p12 can sign builds as you. Apple hands
# a .p8 over exactly ONCE, so the copy on disk is the only copy, and the
# temptation to "just keep it with the project" is exactly how it gets pushed.
# Keep them in a password manager instead. Added 2026-08-19.
*.p8
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
*.mobileprovision
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest

# Google Cloud service account keys. These arrive as JSON, so no extension rule
# can catch them the way *.p8 does without also ignoring package.json and the
# fifteen hundred other JSON files in this repo. Listed below are the shapes
# Google actually emits: the older api-NNNN-NNNN-XXXX.json from the Play
# credentials flow, and the newer PROJECT-KEYID.json from Cloud console. Either
# one grants publishing and financial access to the Play listing, and this repo
# is PUBLIC. Keep the real file outside the repo and delete it after upload.
# Added 2026-08-22 while connecting RevenueCat to Google Play.
api-*.json
bolo-503815-*.json
gcp-*.json
play-*.json
*service-account*.json
*-key.json

# Campaign zips are rebuildable from campaign-duo/ by gen-duo-campaign.mjs.
# The PNGs are committed (same as covers/); the 13MB archive of them is not.
artifacts/bolo-social-clips/*.zip

# Preflight sheets from scripts/src/previewWritingDemo.ts. Look at them, do not commit them.
writing-demo-*.html
